# Keep only source; ignore generated weights (12GB), refs, and compiled binaries.
*
!*.cpp
!*.hpp
# CUDA sources. build.sh COMPILES these (nvcc p3sam_heads_cuda.cu for image_to_rig /
# test_p3sam_segment / p3sam_retopo; svae_cuda.o linked into pixal3d) — without this line the build
# depends on files git is configured never to see, and a clean clone does not compile.
!*.cu
# Patches applied to a SUBMODULE at configure time. ggml/src/ggml-cuda/CMakeLists.txt applies
# flash_attention_native.patch to thirdparty/flash_attention by absolute path when
# GGML_PIXAL_FA2=ON (which is how ggml/build-cuda13 and build-hymo are both configured), and
# FATAL_ERRORs if the tree is neither pristine nor already patched. Without this line the patch is
# untracked, a fresh clone has no file to apply, and the CUDA configure step dies — the same class
# of clean-clone break the *.cu line above exists to prevent.
!*.patch
# NOTE: *.md is deliberately NOT whitelisted. This is a public repo, and handoff/status docs go stale
# in place, then burn an agent's context before it touches anything. Working notes live in the
# gitignored /notes/ dir at the repo root instead.
!*.sh
!*.py
!.gitignore
# shootout/ geometry-eval prep (scripts + docker config only; outputs live on /mnt/hdd, not here)
!shootout/
!shootout/*.sh
!shootout/*.py
!shootout/*.txt
!shootout/Dockerfile*
!shootout/*.requirements.txt
